    "created_at": "2020-05-19T20:54:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-05-19T20:54:01Z",
    "body": "(Oh I see, I was confused.)\r\n\r\nSo the idea here is to remove the block axis fit-content because... most of the time it won't have an effect, so it would be simpler?\r\n\r\nThe compatibility impact of this (for Chrome) would then be that... if someone manually styled their dialog as non-block, it would no longer fit-content? I guess the most likely other display values would be flex or grid...\r\n\r\nAlso, I can no longer find a definition of `fit-content`, only `fit-content()`. So I guess the spec is just outdated in that way too? Chrome uses `-webkit-fit-content` in its UA stylesheet...",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
